EXTENSION "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_TheLowlands_HenriDeToursFollowerOfJerbiton" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Guardians of the Forests - Henri de Tours, follower of Jerbiton"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Guardians_of_the_Forests_Core_Ext"

    # Henri de Tours, follower of Jerbiton (Chapter Seven: The Lowlands, p71): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t4830c649db8bc05bb31946 ^"Henri de Tours, follower of Jerbiton" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t86c663470ee73ae0f109ac ^"Oculus Septentrionalis"]
            ^"Age" STRING "66 (Master)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Ambitious +3, Diplomatic +3, Scheming +2"
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 71
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Henri de Tours is a corpulent and sociable man, dressed splendidly as befits his status as probably the wealthiest merchant in Lübeck (which makes him one of the wealthiest men — at least among commoners — in the whole of Germany). He is well regarded among the city’s burghers as a cultured and able administrator and diplomat. Apprenticed in the Normandy Tribunal, he joined the covenant not long after its founding, and as the oldest remaining member now serves as disceptator. He plans that his familial dynasty will lead it for many generations to come. Henri is a master of Mentem magics, although the more he learns of that Art, the less inclined he becomes towards using it directly. He employs higher magnitude Mentem effects to increase the subtlety, not the raw power, of his magics (see his sample spell on page 72).\n\nBrunhilda, Henri’s wife, is a matronly and insightful woman originating from Sweden. They first met when Henri was a young magus, freshly arrived in Lübeck, and eager to explore the Baltic. His first encounter with the magical folk of Scandinavia set him on the course of love, not war, and the two have been married for more than thirty years. Brunhilda has the power of divination — like Norse wise women she can enter a trance, and send her spirit, in the shape of an animal, far and wide — although her magical powers are not broad enough to qualify her as a member of the Order of Hermes. The magi of the covenant, however, mostly regard her as their equal. Indeed, she is more active than Henri in the covenant’s day-to-day organization. Her divinatory abilities are put to good use as, Henri displays an uncanny knack for choosing the right cargoes and the right ports, at the right times."
    }

}
